# Dependencies (package-lock.json IS committed — it is the supply-chain record).
node_modules/

# ANDROID NATIVE PROJECT — committed (standard Capacitor convention: the
# native shell is checked in; only its build outputs and the payload
# Capacitor copies in at sync time are ignored — see android/.gitignore,
# which `cap add android` generates and which already excludes build/,
# .gradle/, local.properties, *.apk/*.aab, capacitor-cordova-android-plugins
# (regenerated from node_modules), app/src/main/assets/public (copied from
# www/), and the generated capacitor.config.json/capacitor.plugins.json.
#
# TRACK B phase 1 (2026-08-28) built this tree for real: a headless
# Temurin JDK 17 (Gradle launcher) + JDK 21 (required by
# @capacitor/android's Java 21 source/target compatibility) + Android
# commandline-tools (platform-tools, platforms;android-35,
# build-tools;35.0.0/34.0.0) were installed outside the repo under
# ~/android-sdk and ~/jdks, and `./gradlew assembleDebug` produced a real
# APK (see docs — the APK itself is never committed, only regenerable
# build output). No device testing, signing, or release build has
# happened yet; see the mobile-production branch notes for exact status.
# Regenerate from scratch with `npm run add:android`, which runs the
# portable-artifact gate before and the packaged-payload gate after.
# (Its own android/.gitignore, not this file, does the actual excluding.)

# iOS NATIVE PROJECT — still deliberately NOT committed.
#
# `npx cap add ios` scaffolds a large Xcode tree from the Capacitor
# template and then copies the www/ payload into it. It was verified to
# run in this environment previously (see
# docs/postlaunch/mobile-v1-scaffold.md) and the copied payload was proven
# byte-identical to the repository sources by
# `node tools/sync-portable.js --check-packaged`, but unlike android/ as of
# TRACK B phase 1 it has never been BUILT or reviewed here — no Xcode, no
# CocoaPods in this environment — and committing an unbuilt, unreviewed
# native tree would imply a level of verification that does not exist.
# Regenerate with `npm run add:ios`; it runs the portable-artifact gate
# before and the packaged-payload gate after.
ios/
